  "summary": "Tracing every net and value on all four sheets (root, MCU, thermocouples, power) reproduces the specification exactly: the TPS2121 mux (IN1=+12V, IN2=+5V, OUT=VBUS, PR1/OV1/OV2/CP2/ST/GND to GND, R12=51.1k on ILIM, C5=10nF on SS), the AP63203WU buck (FB tied to +3V3, L1=3.9uH, C13=100nF, C9/C10=22uF, C11=10uF), the TPS1H200 high-side switch (VS=+12V, IN/DIAG_EN=GPIO1/HEATER, CL and GND/EP to GND, FAULT only to TP6, OUT to J6), the three MAX31855 channels on a shared SCK/SO bus with independent CS0/CS1/CS2 and 1uF decouplers, the USB-C CC pulldowns (R1/R7=5.1k), the fan-tach TVS/pull-up network (R2/R11=10k, D4/D5/D6 D_TVS), and the WS2812 (D1, C12=1uF, DIN on the LED net). The only discrepancies the spec flags (D7 being a generic 'D' rather than D_TVS, the unmonitored FAULT pin, the leftover LM73100/MPM3606 library parts, the LED placeholder) are explicitly documented as known properties of the reference build, not anomalies, and the schematic matches the firmware's documented GPIO usage. No deviation from the intended design is supported by the drawing."
